  data: {
    LLM: "For Beginners:\n1. Avoid taking the Queen of Spades (pig) at all costs\n2. Try to take the Jack of Diamonds (sheep) for positive points\n3. Be careful with the Ten of Clubs - it can multiply your penalties\n4. Consider exposing cards only if you have strong control of that suit\n\n1. Track which hearts have been played\n2. Decide whether to shoot for all hearts (+200) or avoid them\n3. Use the exposing rule strategically - expose to double positive cards, or to protect yourself from being forced to take penalties\n4. Lead suits where you have the exposed card to avoid playing it\n\n1. Calculate exact probabilities of who holds which cards\n2. Bluff by exposing cards you don't need to protect\n3. Coordinate with partner in partnership play\n4. Read opponents' exposing decisions for information\n5. Complex endgame decisions about whether to take all hearts",
